From: NAOS maintainers <naos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Continue DTB search when libfdt returns a null property

The native Yocto pylibfdt binding can raise TypeError instead of
FdtException when getprop tries to convert a null value into a bytearray.
Handle this at the property lookup so the search continues into child
nodes.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/qcom_capsule_tool/patch_capsule_cert.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/qcom_capsule_tool/patch_capsule_cert.py b/src/qcom_capsule_tool/patch_capsule_cert.py
--- a/src/qcom_capsule_tool/patch_capsule_cert.py
+++ b/src/qcom_capsule_tool/patch_capsule_cert.py
@@ -262,7 +262,7 @@ def _find_cert_node(
         try:
             fdt.getprop(node_off, prop_name)
             return path
-        except libfdt.FdtException:
+        except (libfdt.FdtException, TypeError):
             pass
         child = _fdt_first_subnode(fdt, node_off)
         while child >= 0:
